1 For throwing the checked exception we need to mention in method signature with throws


 public OrderDTO createOrder(OrderDTO orderDTO) throws IOException {
        log.info("Creating new order for user ID: {}", orderDTO.getUserId());

        // VALIDATE ORDER DATA
        if (orderDTO.getItems() == null || orderDTO.getItems().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IOException();
        }

2 For throwing the unchecked exception we no need to mention in method signature with throws

public OrderDTO createOrder(OrderDTO orderDTO) {
        log.info("Creating new order for user ID: {}", orderDTO.getUserId());

        // VALIDATE ORDER DATA
        if (orderDTO.getItems() == null || orderDTO.getItems().isEmpty()) {
            throw new RuntimeException();
        }

3 We can create exception by extending RuntimeException(unchecked) or extending Exception (both unchecked and checked)  also
